

- We extracted unique RNA45S morphs from the fasta file 
- we created a gff file using bedfile of coordinates and gff3 file in Data/assemblies/T2T/
-  bedtools intersect -a Unique_variants_annotation.bed -b  /gpfs/projects/bsc83/Data/assemblies/T2T/chm13.draft_v2.0.gene_annotation.gff3 -wao  >> overlap.bed
- First 5 columns of file overlap.bed were of  Unique_variants_annotation.bed , so we removed them --> NO WE NEED TO KEEP NAMES OF OPERONS !! 
- to sort the gff file we used : sort -k1,1V -k4,4n -k5,5rn -k3,3r overlap.gff > overlap_sorted.gff
 
